egory, never a name. An edition outside the universe lists its year, tier, split tier, use and recorded results","finish_time_universe":"plan decision D22: an edition whose tier is stamped or stamped_weaker_source, or partial with the release’s finishes between 95% and 105% of the official count (both ends included), and that the edition policy does not list as selected_field, mixed_distance_list, incomplete_ingestion or unreconciled_hold; any split tier","flags":"virtual, cancelled, placeholder: the registry flags the title or place (virtual_in_title, cancelled_in_title, placeholder_place) or the notes file flags the race; not_a_marathon_title: the registry finds no marathon word in the title and another event named in it, or the notes file flags it; hand_cycle_title: the registry’s reviewed flag (the title is never printed beside a runner); mountain_or_trail and two_races are for information; title_misleads: the registry’s reviewed flag platform_title_misleads (the timing platform’s title does not describe the marathon results under it: a list shows the label and the place of such a race, never the title). The notes file may clear a flag the rule gives, with its evidence. A race with virtual, cancelled, placeholder, not_a_marathon_title or hand_cycle_title has no page unless the notes file records the lead’s ruling that allows it","left_out":"a race with no live edition (every edition set aside as a copy) is left out of `races`: it has no results to list. Its editions are kept under `left_out`, so that every edition with rows is in the file exactly once","order":"races are in registry order (by race id); a race’s editions by year","page":"course = 3 or more counted editions, or one of the 27 course pages the site had before this adoption whatever it has left; results = not a course page, 3 or more badge-verified editions (stamped or stamped_weaker_source) of at least 100 recorded results each, and at least 3000 recorded results in all; row = every other race. An edition set aside as a copy counts toward nothing","race":"a race is an entry of the frozen race registry; its label is the pipeline’s `city`, its slug the registry’s, shown only when the race has a page","reading":"median finish in a typical verified year = the median of the edition medians over the race’s badge-verified editions of the finish-time universe with at least 100 finishes; stated only with 3 or more such editions, else null. Where the registry gives a label a series note, the reading is per series and the label has none","results":"recorded results = written rows of the edition; finishes = written rows with a finish time","timing":"the producer’s timing basis classed as lib/tiers.ts classes it: chip (chip or net time), chip_fallback (chip or net time where the source has one, else gun or clock time), gun, mixed or not_stated","universe":"every marathon edition with at least one written row in the adapted input (an edition of the release with no row never appears)","use":"counted = the edition policy counts it (it supplies pooled pacing statistics); own_record = not counted, but a record keeps its own pacing view; recorded_times_only = every other edition; `category` is the policy’s category of an edition that is not counted"},"schema_version":1,"scripts":{"analysis/build_races.py":"a4dbe6529f3773fae914f37204181a492b41a440992d5d92fa47f0c0c7f0bc5a","analysis/races_common.py":"77b063fbab0cb6d88196c0ff69952c6f014579b823ad6646118cc11f913d7492"}}
